(a) The order of business at all regular meetings shall be as follows:
(1) Approval of minutes of last meeting;
(2) Corrections, if any, to be made in the minutes;
(3) Unfinished business;
(4) New business;
(5) Other business.
(b) If the mayor and city council directs any matter to be the special business of a future meeting, that matter shall have precedence over all other business at that future meeting.
(c) No proposition shall be entertained by the mayor and city council until it has been seconded, and every proposition shall, when required by the mayor or any member, be reduced to writing.
(Code 1985, § 2-1-13; Code 2004, § 30.04)

